<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd"
  identifier="sat-c1-u01-archaic-pilot-s3" title="Word Parts" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">

  <qti-response-declaration identifier="R1" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>B</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="STAGE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>q1</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="C_TEACH" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>on</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="C_Q1" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>on</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FB1" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>

  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="on" outcome-identifier="C_TEACH" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body>
        <h4>The pieces</h4>
<p><strong>Root &#8212; archa-:</strong> ancient, old (from Greek arkhaios 'ancient, old-fashioned,' itself built on arkhē, 'beginning, origin')</p>
        <p><span style="color:#1d4ed8">Suffix &#8212; -ic:</span> characteristic of, having the quality of</p>
        <p><strong>Put it together:</strong> Archa- (ancient, old — Greek arkhaios, built on arkhē, 'beginning') + -ic (characteristic of) builds the meaning literally: having the character of ancient times — so old-fashioned it seems to belong to an earlier era. Note the spelling: the Greek root keeps its 'ch,' but it is pronounced like 'k' (ar-KAY-ik).</p>
        <p><strong>Use the root in a new word: archetype:</strong> Architecture students traveled to Chicago to sketch the building regarded as the archetype of the modern skyscraper.</p>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="on" outcome-identifier="C_Q1" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body>
        <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="R1" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
          <qti-prompt>The words "archaic" and "archetype" share the Greek root 'arch-.' Considering that, what does "archetype" most nearly mean?</qti-prompt>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">the study of ancient life through objects people left behind</qti-simple-choice>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="B">the first model of something, which later versions follow</qti-simple-choice>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="C">a stored collection of old records and documents</qti-simple-choice>
          <qti-simple-choice identifier="D">an old-fashioned word or phrase surviving from an earlier age</qti-simple-choice>
        </qti-choice-interaction></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="q1A" outcome-identifier="FB1" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Studying ancient life through leftover objects is archaeology - arkhaios plus -logy, 'study of.' An archetype is not a field of study; its -type ending points at a pattern, not a science.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="q1C" outcome-identifier="FB1" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>A stored collection of old records is an archive - from arkheion, the record office where a city's past was kept. An archetype is a single thing, not a roomful of documents.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="q1D" outcome-identifier="FB1" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>An old-fashioned expression still lingering in the language is an archaism - the closest cousin to archaic itself. An archetype is not a leftover from the past; its -type half does different work.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="q1correct" outcome-identifier="FB1" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Right - arch- carries the Greek arkhe, 'beginning, origin,' and an archetype is the beginning-stamp: arkhe plus typos, 'stamp, model,' the first pattern that everything after it follows. Archaic looks back at the same starting point - so old it belongs to the beginnings.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="q1incorrect" outcome-identifier="FB1" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite. All four options reach back to the Greek arkh- family, so age alone cannot settle it. The second half of archetype is -type, a stamp or pattern - ask what kind of thing a stamp is to everything printed from it.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>

  <qti-response-processing>
    <qti-response-condition>
      <qti-response-if>
        <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="STAGE"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">q1</qti-base-value></qti-match>
        <qti-response-condition>
          <qti-response-if>
            <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="R1"/><qti-correct identifier="R1"/></qti-match>
            <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FB1"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">q1correct</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
            <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="SCORE"><qti-base-value base-type="float">1</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
            <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="STAGE"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">done</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
            <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="completionStatus"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">completed</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
          </qti-response-if>
          <qti-response-else>
            <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FB1"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">q1incorrect</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
            <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="completionStatus"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">incomplete</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
            <qti-response-condition>
              <qti-response-if>
                <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="R1"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">A</qti-base-value></qti-match>
                <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FB1"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">q1A</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
              </qti-response-if>
            </qti-response-condition>
            <qti-response-condition>
              <qti-response-if>
                <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="R1"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">C</qti-base-value></qti-match>
                <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FB1"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">q1C</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
              </qti-response-if>
            </qti-response-condition>
            <qti-response-condition>
              <qti-response-if>
                <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="R1"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">D</qti-base-value></qti-match>
                <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FB1"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">q1D</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
              </qti-response-if>
            </qti-response-condition>
          </qti-response-else>
        </qti-response-condition>
      </qti-response-if>
      <qti-response-else>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="completionStatus"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">completed</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      </qti-response-else>
    </qti-response-condition>
  </qti-response-processing>
</qti-assessment-item>
